  "worked_solution": "We notice that $E$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $E$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $E$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $ER$ has dimensions $3\\times 3:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3}={ER}_{3\\times 3}\n$$",
